    "A trade agreement meets a constitutional obstacle. The United States and Ecuador signed an Agreement on Reciprocal Trade on March 13, 2026. On October 16, Ecuador's Constitutional Court determined that the agreement requires approval by the National Assembly before ratification. The signature is a diplomatic milestone, not proof that every provision is now legally operating.",
